  "_comment": "The route limit covers the pre-join entrance (#712); SpaceCall loads the admitted call after Join (#730), and builds its join client from the generated ChalkPublicApi (only the unauthenticated /v1/public operations), so the MCP OAuth contract (#814) stays out of the route. The route measures about 205.5 KiB and its ceiling is 217 KiB, down from 219. Five fresh-context bundle-only runs per revision on Linux x64, 8-core Intel Xeon, Node 24.19.0, pnpm 12.8.1 and Chromium 151.0.7922.34 give non-board JavaScript gzip min/median/max of 386.486/386.486/386.486 KiB on master 35a9d072c and 386.560/386.560/386.560 KiB with send recovery. Validating the call path with Effect Schema instead of zod, which also removes zod and its English locale from the call JavaScript, cut 2.1 KiB (386.5 to 384.5 KiB on the same machine), so the non-board ceiling went down from 387 to 385 KiB. Board, CSS, timing, video-quality and leak limits and the historical timing baseline remain unchanged. The route limit alone falls, from 219 to 217 KiB.",
